+ *   S2  `onPress` forgives — a tap, then a real MOUSE click (press and release) about 100 ms on,
+ *       with the tap's own click withheld (WebKit's delivery; a hybrid touch-and-mouse device)
+ *   S3  `onKey` forgives — a tap, then Enter on the mark about 100 ms on (same delivery)
+ *   S1  `onClick` pays — the tap's own click arrives (Chromium's delivery, or one click labelled
+ *       `mouse` 60 ms after the release, the RELABEL delivery, in both engines), then a press-less
+ *       click about 100 ms on
+ * The pass-8 critic's costs, each the negative's: S1 swallowed a press-less click at +109 ms,
+ * S2 a mouse click at +111-120 ms, S3 an Enter at +117-143 ms. The clean arm toggles each time.
