+    // keep the full hover + focus-within disclosure (the UI-6 keyboard path is fine-pointer).
+    //
+    // THE LINE THAT USED TO END THIS PARAGRAPH WAS FALSE, AND ITS OWN CODE REFUTED IT (CH-70).
+    // It read "a coarse keyboard user still opens via the trigger's Enter
+    // (@keydown.enter=toggle)". That handler used `.stop` — `stopPropagation`, never
+    // `preventDefault` — so Enter ran the toggle AND the activation click the button synthesises
+    // from it: twice, netting zero. Measured 2026-09-18 on both engines at a coarse viewport:
+    // focus the trigger, `aria-expanded false`; Enter, `false`; Space, `true`. The handler is
+    // deleted, and the true sentence is the simple one: a keyboard user on any pointer opens
